      "content": "A heating pad can be a great idea, it'll help relax the muscles and reduce the hardness. Just be sure to set it to a low setting, you don't want to overdo it and cause any further irritation. Also, try to take it easy, avoid heavy lifting or bending, and get plenty of rest. The lightheadedness and racing heart are probably just a side effect of the anesthesia wearing off, but if it persists, you might want to consider a gentle walk around the block to get the blood flowing.",
